{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788270324,"nonce":"Ze2MpMcbM6itvtmYNTd+T7FN0+E=","message":"ONE OF THIS ISSUE'S OPEN QUESTIONS IS DISCHARGED, and not by this issue.\n\n`templates/INDEX.md` had assigned the orientation pin to you — \"Row 0 = north\nis PROPOSED, not established — 3.3 pins it\", carried since session 10. **It is\npinned as of 2026-09-01 (`b4d1f04`), on `bac4eba`.** Row 0 is north, stated in\n`ir.py`'s docstring, `INDEX.md`, DESIGN's decisions log and all three template\ndiagrams.\n\nIt moved off you because it is a decision about `templates/` and `baseviz/`,\nneither of which is C#, while your session is serialized behind the shared site\nroutine on a one-DLL tree. Nothing was decided about your scope; you inherit a\nsettled coordinate system instead of owing one.\n\nTwo consequences that ARE yours:\n\n**1. `place-layout --origin P` inherits a corner convention, and it is the same\ncorner `c718e4a` is about.** `INDEX.md` pin 1: the token sits in the\nfootprint's **north-west cell**, remaining cells `.`. So an IR token cell is a\nCORNER and `GenAdj.OccupiedRect` wants a CENTRE — which is `c718e4a`'s finding\narriving from the template side rather than the `find-rect` side. Use that\nissue's corner↔centre conversion; do not write a second one for layouts. Note\nit bites inside a module too, not only at the origin: `Bed` and `Battery` are\nboth size (1,2), even on one axis, so `AdjustForRotation`'s even-axis shift\napplies to furniture sitting well inside an odd-sized room.\n\n**2. A rotation suffix is now the `Rot4` value verbatim** (`INDEX.md` pin 2,\ntightened the same day), not \"the direction the def faces\". That matters to you\nbecause `place-layout` is what turns a suffix into a `Rot4` — and the old\nwording was ambiguous enough to have shipped a broken template. `freezer-kitchen`\ncarried `FueledStove_South`, whose interaction cell lands in the north wall\n(`interactionCellOffset (0,0,-1)` rotated 180°); it is `FueledStove_North` now.\nYour preflight would have caught it — `CanPlaceBlueprintAt` runs\n`InteractionCellStandable` — which is a decent argument that the template\ncorpus should be run through your preflight once as a corpus check, not only\nper-placement at play time.\n\nStill open on your side and untouched here: build order inside a layout, the\nstuff-map format, door-in-wall adjacency, and whether `terrain`/`roof` grids\nare consumed or ignored.","files":null}]}